   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau to transfer ownership\nof certain parkland to the village of Freeport",
    "basePrintNo": "S5566",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5566-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5566\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau\nto transfer ownership of certain parkland to the village of Freeport\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill authorizes Nassau County (the \"County\") to convey Cow Meadow\nPark and Preserve (\"Cow Meadow\"), located in the Village of Freeport\n(the \"Village\"), to the Village.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. authorizes the county of Nassau to convey Cow Meadow to the\nVillage of Freeport for use as a public park.\n\nSection 2. describes the boundaries and area of the land being trans-\nferred.\n\nSection 3. provides that the facilities and land being transferred will\nbe maintained, owned and operated by the village of Freeport.\n\nSection 4. provides that when availability of the public parkland is\nlimited, the use of such land or facilities must be determined based on\nan equitable method that prioritizes use for free or in exchange for\nfees commensurate with the administrative costs of such use.\n\nSection 5. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation simply transfers ownership of Cow Meadow from the\nNassau County to the Village of Freeport. The transfer will enable the\nconsolidation of services, improve efficiency, and create new recre-\national opportunities for county and village residents. The County and\nVillage believe this transfer is in the best interest of the taxpayers\nof their respective municipalities.\n\nThe Village intends to improve Cow Meadow through capital improvements\nsuch as installing additional ballfields and rehabilitating the marina,\nthereby offering additional recreational opportunities for County and\nVillage residents.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately after it shall have become law.\n",
